# Fleet Worker split + Adam API

- Server 2 `fleet-static-worker` = Batches 1–7 live apex. Origin IP `174.136.29.214`. Do not move B1–7 onto server 1.
- Server 1 `fleet-static-worker-server-1` = new batches after B1–7. Origin IP `165.140.157.43`.
- Both share KV `HTML_FLEET` + R2 `fleet-static-assets`. Keys: `{host}:html:` / `{host}:asset:`. Preview uses `static.{domain}:…`.

Adam `POST …/provision-originless` (and `/scrape` with `"fleet": true`):

- Omit `workerName` → attaches `static.{domain}/*` to `fleet-static-worker`. Use for B1–7 only.
- `"workerName":"fleet-static-worker-server-1"` → same scrape and preview-only route on server 1. Use for new sites.
- Never omit `workerName` on a new-batch domain (it would land on server 2).
- API does not touch apex/www. Apex cutover stays on us after QA.
